    "composite_objective": 0.7246,
    "baseline_composite_objective": 0.7135,
    "delta_vs_baseline": -0.0111,
    "accepted": false,
    "reason": "Correctly specified as a REPLACEMENT for the raw form group, this is clearly worse (composite 0.7246 vs baseline 0.7135, delta -0.0111). Per-tournament it is not even consistently worse — it improves 2002/2006/2014 marginally but is dragged down hard by 2010 (-0.061 vs baseline) and 2022 (-0.027) — exactly the \"spectacular on some tournaments, poor on others\" pattern Phase 8 says to avoid selecting for. REJECTED. The original EXP-002 (additive) result of a threshold-boundary +0.0050 improvement is now understood to be a 3-extra-mostly-redundant-columns effect, not evidence that a compact form representation beats the noisy one — both EXP-002 and this corrected test are excluded from the final feature set."
